content:
{
  "asset": "P-102 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-19870, on the filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal leakage: the steady drip at approximately one drop per second matches the manual symptom 'Leakage at shaft seal', for which the corrective action is mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check. No allowable numerical seal-leakage rate is documented, so a numerical pass/fail comparison cannot be made.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: on Figure 3's bearing-housing velocity scale, the reported drive-end reading of 2.1 mm/s is below the 2.8 mm/s RMS Zone A/B boundary and therefore falls within Zone A (0.0–2.8 mm/s RMS). It is below Zone C, restricted operation starting at 4.5 mm/s RMS, and Zone D, the stop-pump zone starting at 7.1 mm/s RMS. This is only the drive-end result; the manual requires readings on both housings and classification of the highest.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing temperature: the applicable manual limits are normal up to 70 °C, alarm at 80 °C and trip at 90 °C, with bearing temperature measured on the housing surface. The reported 66 °C is within the normal range, 14 °C below alarm and 24 °C below trip. It does not trigger SSP-07's requirement for a priority-1 work order within the shift, which applies above the manufacturer's alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Operational decision: on the reported readings, neither the highest-vibration-zone immediate-stop rule nor the above-temperature-alarm P1 rule is triggered. The active seal leakage nevertheless requires seal replacement and an alignment check, so plan a P2 isolated repair rather than an emergency stop; reassess if the second-housing vibration reading changes the highest-zone classification.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked mechanical-seal faces, listed first in the manual's causes for shaft-seal leakage; confirm by inspection when the seal is withdrawn.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The seal may have run dry. Check the Plan 11 flush arrangement from pump discharge and any evidence of dry running; the manual explicitly prohibits dry running.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. Check alignment against parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before repair, confirm that the reported vibration is mm/s RMS, measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings, and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. Also confirm the housing-surface temperature. If the highest vibration reading is in Zone D, apply the immediate-stop and reliability-engineer notification control.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Investigate the leakage cause without running the pump dry: verify the Plan 11 seal-flush supply from pump discharge and record any evidence of dry running.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Apply the chemical PPE and isolation controls. Electrically isolate and lock out/tag out at the MCC, mechanically isolate suction and discharge valves, drain and vent before the line-break permit, and isolate and drain the pump for seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Prepare the removal lift: the back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, exceeding the 25 kg threshold. Obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Using the approved lift, remove the back pull-out assembly. Its back pull-out design allows removal without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller, then withdraw the mechanical seal and sleeve.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the removed seal faces for wear or cracking and inspect the sleeve for scoring, recording the findings. If scoring is found, obtain an applicable disposition before proceeding because the evidence provides no scoring acceptance limit for this serial number.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit one new HF3-450 mechanical seal and one new casing gasket. HF3-450 remains the specified seal for pumps below serial HF3-22000, including HF3-19870.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten all disturbed fasteners to Table 5 with lightly oiled threads: M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm; M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm; M10 seal gland nuts to 25 Nm for HF3-450 on this asset; and M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm if disturbed. Do not substitute the service bulletin's 30 Nm gland torque.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool and correct it to parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm. Laser alignment is mandatory after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before operation, verify the Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and never run the seal dry. Following repair, resume weekly vibration-velocity measurements on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450",
      "description": "Mechanical seal for HF-300 serial HF3-19870; pumps below HF3-22000 continue to use HF3-450.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "Not specified in evidence",
      "description": "New casing gasket required during mechanical-seal replacement; obtain the correct gasket before starting the repair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves: P-102 is within pumps P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line, which are chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For work inside the pump or on its seal, provide electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanically isolate both the suction and discharge valves before seal or internal pump work.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Obtain a line-break permit, draining and venting the line first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For the 68 kg back pull-out assembly, use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment; this exceeds the 25 kg lifting-control threshold.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If subsequent measurements place the highest housing vibration in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, Zone D, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. The reported 2.1 mm/s reading is not in that zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement standard allowance: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians, equal to 8.0 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-alignment standard allowance: 1.5 hours with 1 technician, planned in addition because the seal-leakage troubleshooting action requires an alignment check.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Total planned standard labour for seal replacement and laser alignment: 9.5 technician-hours. No additional allowance is documented for unforeseen sleeve or bearing work.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal selection and gland torque: Table 5 specifies 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, while SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, specifies cartridge seal HF3-450B and 30 Nm. The bulletin applies only to serial HF3-22000 and above and explicitly states that lower serials continue using HF3-450 and Table 5. P-102 is serial HF3-19870, so the manual/lower-serial instruction applies: use HF3-450 and 25 Nm with lightly oiled threads, not HF3-450B and 30 Nm. The bulletin's 0.1 mm sleeve-scoring/HF3-455 replacement instruction is likewise not applied to this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What allowable mechanical-seal leakage rate, if any, applies, and what response time is required for this P2 repair? The evidence gives no numerical leakage limit and no P2/P3 response-time definitions; it only directs corrective action for shaft-seal leakage and defines a temperature-based P1 trigger. (C09, C15)",
    "Is the reported 2.1 mm/s vibration value an RMS velocity, and what is the non-drive-end housing reading? Both housings must be measured and the highest reading classified on the mm/s RMS scale. (C06, C07)",
    "Which cause is confirmed by inspection: worn/cracked seal faces, dry running or misalignment? No seal inspection, flush/dry-running history or measured alignment result is supplied. (C02, C09)",
    "If the sleeve is scored, what scoring acceptance limit and replacement sleeve part apply to serial HF3-19870? The manual requires inspection but gives no limit, while the 0.1 mm/HF3-455 instruction in SB-2026-014 is restricted to serial HF3-22000 and above. (C10, C13)",
    "What is the part number of the required new casing gasket? Seal replacement requires a new gasket, but no gasket part number is provided. (C10)"
  ]
}
